// Title: Potential RDP Tunneling Via SSH
// Sigma ID: f7d7ebd5-a016-46e2-9c54-f9932f2d386d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-10-12 | Modified: 2023-01-25
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1572
// Description: Execution of ssh.exe to perform data exfiltration and tunneling through RDP
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.absolomb.com/2018-01-26-Windows-Privilege-Escalation-Guide/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ssh_rdp_tunneling.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\ssh.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains ":3389"
